CM_ "DashKit DBC for the new-generation Model Y (Juniper). Reverse-engineered from comma route 077b771458fd542f/000000a9--5f9f91a356 (2026-09-22, 16:49-17:05 local) against the annotated action timeline, using dbc/bus_1_tesla_vehicle.dbc as the blueprint and the Tesla FW 2026.2 signal-name dataset for naming. Comma bus 1 = Tesla vehicle bus (BU_ VEH), comma bus 0/2 = party bus (BU_ PARTY). The chassis bus (DashKit bus 0) is not part of a comma log, so chassis placement is unverified. Bytesum checksum = (id_lo + id_hi + sum of data bytes except the checksum byte) & 0xFF.";
CM_ BO_ 585 "CHANGED. DLC 3 -> 4. Byte 0 is now a CRC (SCCM_leftStalkCrc, Tesla's own name): the legacy bytesum matched 0/2000 frames, no CRC-8/CRC-16 variant matched either; the value is XOR-linear in the data bytes with a nonlinear per-counter term. The firmware cannot synthesize a valid frame until the algorithm is known. Bits 20-31 are a 12-bit stalk angle (rest ~1800, right tap ~1839, left tap ~1762, 4095 = SNA); its LSB jitters, which is why bit 20 looked like a button. Turn stalk taps at 16:53:31 (right blinker) and 16:53:34 (left blinker) read 2 (UP_1) and 6 (DOWN_1). SCCM_washWipeButtonStatus (bits 14-15) never changed during the 16:49:45-16:50:13 wiper-menu session: the Juniper wiper button reports through VCLEFT_switchStatus.VCLEFT_swcWiperButtonState instead.";
CM_ SG_ 585 SCCM_leftStalkCrc "Not the Tesla bytesum any more. Empirical model: crc = L(data) XOR K[counter], L linear over GF(2); K[0..15] observed = ad de 1c e5 e5 55 7a 68 09 88 d4 1e 0c 25 99 f8 for payload byte2=0x80 byte3=0x70. Flipping bit 20 XORs 0xE0.";
CM_ SG_ 585 SCCM_turnIndicatorStalkAngle "New 12-bit stalk position (raw ticks, 4095 = SNA). Observed 1761-1840, centre 1800.";
CM_ BO_ 962 "UNCHANGED layout, DLC 8, no checksum. Verified: swcLeftScrollTicks (mux 1, 16|6 signed) +1 x5 while scrolling the wiper speed up (16:49:50-16:49:59) and -1 x5 scrolling down (16:50:01-16:50:09); frontBuckleSwitch (mux 0, 48|2) = 2 ON for the whole drive. NEW: VCLEFT_swcWiperButtonState (mux 1, 22|2) = 2 HARD_PRESS for 180 ms at 16:49:47.99, immediately followed by a single wipe in VCFRONT_status (wiperState 4->6, wiperSpeed 1->2 at 16:49:48.26) and the wiper menu opening. This is the button the wiper-off automation should inject on Juniper; it has no checksum.";
CM_ SG_ 962 VCLEFT_swcWiperButtonState "New on Juniper: wiper button press (0 INACTIVE, 1 SOFT_PRESS, 2 HARD_PRESS, 3 FAULT). Replaces the SCCM_washWipeButtonStatus path.";
CM_ BO_ 1001 "UNCHANGED layout, DLC 8, bytesum checksum verified 2000/2000, counter 52|4. Seen on vehicle and party bus. CAUTION: DAS_wiperSpeed reads 15 (INVALID) the whole drive except while Autopilot was engaged (16:55:18-16:55:30 -> 0), so a wiper-off trigger keyed on DAS_wiperSpeed changes will fire on Autopilot engage/disengage rather than on auto-wipe. Bit 21 (undefined in the blueprint) cleared exactly when the wiper menu opened (16:49:50.28) and is a candidate for DAS_overrideWiperSetting / DAS_autoWiperState (FW 2026.2 names, position unproven).";
CM_ BO_ 991 "LAYOUT UNCHANGED, BUS CHANGED. DLC 8. UI_activeTouchPoints (24|8) read 1/2/3/4 for the 1-4 finger taps at 16:50:19, 16:50:22, 16:50:27, 16:50:32 and UI_touchDetected (17|1) pulsed with each tap. The frame exists ONLY on the party bus (comma bus 0/2) in this log, never on the vehicle bus the firmware decodes it from (used_messages.txt bus 1). On legacy Model 3/Y it was on the vehicle bus (panda reads 0x3DF on bus 1).";
CM_ BO_ 627 "UNCHANGED layout, DLC 8, ~3 Hz, on vehicle and party bus. Verified UI_lockRequest (17|3) = 1 LOCK / 2 UNLOCK pulses of 0.5-0.8 s for the lock icon taps 16:50:47-16:50:59, UI_mirrorFoldRequest (24|2) = 1 RETRACT at 16:51:16 / 2 PRESENT at 16:51:28 (1 s pulses). NOTE: the Juniper UI opens the trunk through UI_vehicleControl2.UI_trunkRequest, UI_remoteClosureRequest (54|2) never toggled during the four trunk requests.";
CM_ BO_ 947 "CHANGED: DLC 2 -> 8 (bit positions of the known signals unchanged). UI_gloveboxRequest (0|1) held for ~3 s at 16:59:10.75 and 16:59:20.92; UI_trunkRequest (1|1) pulsed ~0.7 s at 17:01:28.6, 17:01:35.6, 17:01:45.0, 17:01:50.6. Steady bytes: 80 80 04 30 00 00 a8 80 (bit 15 VCLEFTFeature1, bit 18 userPresent, bit 29 autoRollWindowsOnLock). Bits 37-38 and 56-57 toggled at 17:00:01-17:00:12 (unidentified, probably seat/wheel comfort). The firmware sends UI_vehicleControl2 with the DBC DLC, so the legacy 2-byte frame is the likely reason the glovebox command is ignored on Juniper.";
CM_ BO_ 819 "CHANGED: DLC 4 -> 5. Bits 0-25 unchanged: chargeEnableRequest = 1, acChargeCurrentLimit = 16 A, chargeTerminationPct = 100.0 %. Bit 26 is constantly 1 (unidentified). New bit 36 rose at 17:02:48.75 when a supercharger was selected in navigation and fell at 17:03:01.21 when navigation was cancelled; named UI_cpInletHeaterRequest (FW 2026.2 signal, 1 = AUTO) by inference. Charge port open/close bits were not exercised in the log; the user reports they still work.";
CM_ BO_ 839 "UNCHANGED bits 0-7, DLC 8, 1 Hz. Vehicle bus ID 0x347; the identical payload is also sent on the party bus as 0x082. Supercharger navigation 17:02:48 -> 17:03:01: byte0 0x01 -> 0x02 (navToSupercharger) -> 0x0e (type 3 = V3) -> 0xae (precondition state 1 ACTIVE_HEAT + requestBatteryHeating) -> 0xaf -> 0x01. FW 2026.2 names for the old someValue bytes: A = UI_battPreconditionOnNavPowerReq (int8, 127 SNA, went 0x7f -> 0x50), B = UI_battPreconditionOnNavTargetT (255 SNA, 0xff -> 0xd4), C = UI_ambientTempAtDestination (int8, -128 SNA). New: UI_tripPlanChargingTargetPercent (32|10, 1023 SNA) and UI_energyAtDestination (48|16 signed, 0.01 kWh: 55.61 kWh idle = pack remaining, -327.68 SNA while computing, 53.79 kWh once routed).";
CM_ SG_ 839 UI_someValueA "FW 2026.2: UI_battPreconditionOnNavPowerReq (int8, 126 MAX, 127 SNA). Old name kept for firmware compatibility.";
CM_ SG_ 839 UI_someValueB "FW 2026.2: UI_battPreconditionOnNavTargetT (0 MIN, 254 MAX, 255 SNA). Old name kept for firmware compatibility.";
CM_ SG_ 839 UI_someValueC "FW 2026.2: UI_ambientTempAtDestination (int8, -128 SNA). Old name kept for firmware compatibility.";
CM_ BO_ 755 "CHANGED: DLC 5 -> 8 and BUS CHANGED (party bus only in this log, not on the vehicle bus the firmware injects on). Old bit positions verified: setpoints 0|5 / 8|5 = 22.5 / 23 degC, blowerSegment 16|4 = 11 AUTO, userPowerState 26|3 = 1 ON, UI_hvacReqSecondRowState 29|3 = 1 OFF -> 4 HIGH at 17:02:09.8, 2 LOW at 17:02:14.8, 4 at 17:02:16.7, 1 at 17:02:19.7, 4 at 17:02:22.5, 1 at 17:02:28.0 (rear fan on/off sequence). New UI_hvacReqAutoBlowerLevel (5|3) stepped 0 -> 2 -> 4 -> 2 -> 0 during the 17:00:18-17:00:29 fan adjustments (VERY_LOW/MEDIUM/VERY_HIGH). Bit 59 toggles when the climate panel is open (0x42 <-> 0x4a in byte 7); bytes 4-6 = 00 60 00 unidentified.";
CM_ BO_ 820 "UNCHANGED layout, DLC 8, 2 Hz, vehicle bus. UI_pedalMap (5|2) 0 CHILL -> 1 SPORT at 17:03:14.5, 0 at 17:03:18.1, 1 at 17:03:20.9, 0 at 17:03:22.7 (chill/standard toggles). Bytesum checksum verified 1997/1997, counter 52|4.";
CM_ BO_ 595 "CHANGED: DLC 7 -> 8, now MULTIPLEXED on byte 0 (0 = front vents at ~2 Hz, 1 = second-row vents at ~2 Hz, alternating), and BUS CHANGED (party bus only in this log). Mux 0 bytes 1-6 keep the old meaning (left X/Y/split, right X/Y/split, 0.5 %): during the driver-vent manipulation 16:59:46-16:59:52 in SPLIT mode, byte 2 (left Y) fell 200 -> 123 on the downward drag and byte 3 (left lateral split) went 200 -> 20 (streams to the middle) -> 200 (fully right). New byte 7: UI_ventPanelLeftLateralMode (56|2) 1 SPLIT -> 2 SWING at 16:52:16.5 and 16:52:26.1, back to 1 at 16:52:22.2 and 16:52:29.9; UI_ventPanelRightLateralMode (58|2) 0 SINGLE -> 2 SWING at 16:52:32.4 and 16:52:37.8, back to 0 at 16:52:35.6 and 16:52:40.3 (matches the driver/passenger swing on/off sequence; the timeline stamps are ~5 s later than the CAN). The car has a native swing mode, so the AC-swing automation can set the mode bit instead of sweeping X. Mux 1 payload was constant (c8 b6 a9 c8 00 00 00); its signal order follows the FW 2026.2 listing and is inferred. The firmware's RMW of the 'last live frame' may now grab the mux-1 frame.";
CM_ BO_ 297 "UNCHANGED layout, DLC 8, 100 Hz, vehicle bus. SCCM_steeringAngle (16|14) swept -201.7 .. +182.3 deg during the 16:52:48-16:52:53 wheel turns, SCCM_steeringAngleSpeed (32|14) consistent. CAUTION: byte 0 is no longer the Tesla bytesum (0/2000 match); same unknown CRC family as SCCM_leftStalk. Name kept because the firmware only forwards this frame.";
CM_ BO_ 280 "UNCHANGED layout, DLC 8, 100 Hz, vehicle + party bus. DI_gear (21|3): 1 P -> 4 D at 16:53:01.2 (the 16:53:02 'reverse' note was actually D: no reverse light, speed 0), 1 P at 16:53:07.1, 4 D at 16:53:29.0, 2 R at 16:54:36.0 (speed -5 km/h, reverse light on), 4 D at 16:54:38.8, 2 R 17:01:01.6-17:01:07.0, 1 P at 17:01:24.7. DI_accelPedalPos (32|8, 0.4 %) 0..100 % during the 16:51:58-16:52:04 pedal presses. Bytesum checksum verified.";
CM_ BO_ 599 "UNCHANGED layout, DLC 8, 50 Hz, vehicle + party bus. DI_vehicleSpeed (12|12) 56.56 km/h with DI_uiSpeed = 58 at 16:55:52; negative while reversing. Bytesum checksum verified.";
CM_ BO_ 921 "UNCHANGED layout, DLC 8, 2 Hz. DAS_autopilotState (0|4) = 3 ACTIVE_NOMINAL 16:55:20.7-16:55:30.0 (Autopilot on/off per timeline), 1/2 otherwise; DAS_autopilotHandsOnState (42|4) 1 -> 2 during the engagement. Bytesum checksum verified. Seen only on the party bus (comma 0/2), consistent with the firmware's bus-0 placement.";
CM_ BO_ 905 "UNCHANGED layout, DLC 8, ~2.4 Hz. DAS_lssState (31|3) = 3 while Autopilot was engaged (16:55:20.7-16:55:30.1), 0/1 at standstill, 2/3/7 later in the drive; DAS_accSpeedLimit (0|10) and DAS_activationFailureStatus (14|2) moved around the engagement. Bytesum checksum verified. Seen on the vehicle bus (comma bus 1) only.";
CM_ BO_ 605 "UNVERIFIED / DLC 6 -> 8. Tesla FW 2026.2 calls 0x25D APP_trafficControl (APP_tcControlLightState: 0 NONE 1 RED 2 GREEN 3 YELLOW; APP_tcControlDistance 255 = SNA; state machine, control type...). In this log the party-bus payload was static (37 41 01 06 04 f0 xx 03, only byte 6 jitters +-3) through the yellow->red (16:57:24-25) and red->green (16:57:52) light and both stop-line approaches (16:54:55, 16:55:36), so neither traffic-light colour nor stop-line distance is observable on this car (no Traffic Light & Stop Sign Control). No other message on the party or vehicle bus carried those transitions either. Old signals kept for app compatibility but they decode to garbage here (colour = 6, dist = 0.5 m); treat as unavailable on Juniper.";
CM_ BO_ 994 "UNCHANGED (vehicle-bus copy, DLC 7, ~5 Hz). VCLEFT_turnSignalStatus (4|2) blinked 1/0 at 16:53:36-16:53:38 (left blinker); bit 18 (leftTurnTrailerLightStatus) follows it, bit 20 follows the right blinker. NOTE: 0x3E2 on the party bus is a different 8-byte 1 Hz frame; keep this message on bus 1.";
CM_ BO_ 995 "CHANGED: DLC 2 -> 4. Old bits verified: brakeLightStatus (0|2) = 1 while braking, tailLightStatus 2|2, VCRIGHT_turnSignalStatus (4|2) blinked 1/0 at 16:53:31-16:53:34 (right blinker), reverseLightStatus (6|2) = 1 while in R (16:54:36, 17:01:01). New byte 1 bit 13 was set exactly while reversing and byte 3 bit 29 exactly while the brake light was on: named VCRIGHT_fasciaReverseLightStatus and VCRIGHT_CHMSLLightStatus from the FW 2026.2 signal list (inferred).";
CM_ BO_ 737 "UNCHANGED as far as observable, DLC 8, 62 Hz. Mux-0 wiper fields decoded sensibly during the wiper-menu session (wiperSpeed 1/2/8, wiperState 4/6/7/8/9/10). No door was opened in the log, so anyClosureOpen/anyDoorOpen (bits 49/50, both 0 throughout) are unverified.";
CM_ BO_ 850 "UNCHANGED, DLC 8, 1.5 Hz. Mux 0: nominalFullPackEnergy 81.38 kWh, nominalEnergyRemaining 55.5 kWh, idealEnergyRemaining 55.38 kWh. A new mux index 2 also appears (not decoded).";
CM_ BO_ 594 "UNCHANGED, DLC 8, 10 Hz. maxRegenPower 98 kW, maxDischargePower 293.7 kW at 16:56:00.";
CM_ BO_ 306 "CHANGED: DLC 8 -> 6. BMS_packVoltage (0|16, Tesla now calls it BMS_dcLinkVoltage) 380.69 V, BMS_packCurrent (16|15) 3.4 A, BMS_currentUnfiltered (32|16) 2.95 A at 16:56:00. BMS_chgTimeToFull (48|12) no longer fits in the frame and was removed.";
CM_ BO_ 818 "UNCHANGED, DLC 6, 1 Hz. Mux 0 thermistorTMax 18.0 / TMin 17.5 degC.";
CM_ BO_ 950 "CHANGED: DLC 4 -> 8. DI_odometer (0|32, 0.001 km) = 3651.992 km. New DI_odometerStatusCounter (52|4) and DI_odometerStatusChecksum (56|8, bytesum verified 300/300). Bits 32-51 hold DI_obdDriveCycleStatus (FW 2026.2 name, position unproven, read 0).";
CM_ BO_ 1029 "LAYOUT UNCHANGED (index 0|8 with 56-bit payloads for indices 16/17/18, 4 Hz, vehicle + party bus) but the VIN split changed: index 16 carries only the 3-character WMI right-aligned after four NUL bytes, index 17 carries characters 4-10 and index 18 characters 11-17. An assembler expecting 7+7+3 must skip the NULs / re-order.";

